{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Their tongue and their doings.</b> All their speech and all their deeds are against HaShem." "<b>To defy.</b> The lamed has pataḥ in place of the [missing] hei of the binyan; like it is לנחותם הדרך (Exodus 13:21)." "And the sense of <b>עיני</b> is: in public."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra says the lamed has pataḥ where the construction would require a hei (i.e., להרות → למרות); 'the binyan' refers to the grammatical pattern/form. The gloss '(the missing)' is implied by 'החסר'."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:53.237722013Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}